                <pb facs="0692" n="556" sameAs="frus:frus1929v01/pg556"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">810.79611 Pan American Airways, Inc./380:
                    Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Chargé in France</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Armour</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1929-04-09T17:00:00-05:00">April 9, 1929—5
                    p.m.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p>105. Pan American Airways, Incorporated, is planning to extend its system through
                    the countries of the Caribbean to Cayenne and desires to obtain from the French
                    Government permission to fly over French Guiana, also to refuel and make minor
                    repairs, and to deliver <pb facs="0693" n="557" xml:id="pg557"/> United States
                    mail if awarded concession for that route by the United States Post Office. A
                    representative of the Company is being sent to French Guiana to negotiate
                    permanent operating concession and air mail contract. Please request the French
                    Government to grant temporary authorization valid until replaced by formal
                    contract.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Stimson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
